[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-50b5f005-1185-4325-aac6-594189807b2b\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Mon 17 Nov 2025 14:20 - 14:30 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2025/ase-2025-venue-grand-hall-2\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Grand Hall 2</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Translation</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/saikatdutta1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Saikat Dutta</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"50b5f005-1185-4325-aac6-594189807b2b\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Polyglot: An Extensible Framework to Benchmark Code Translation with LLMs</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Large Language Models (LLMs) show great potential for automating code-related tasks. However, sound assessments are necessary to understand their true capabilities, particularly in code translation, where reliability is crucial. This paper studies the performance of LLMs in code translation by introducing a well-defined, automated, multi-language framework, referred to as Polyglot, that is adaptable to various programming languages and translation scenarios. Leveraging the IBM CodeNet Project, an extensive collection of coding problems in multiple languages, we assess translation quality using syntactic correctness, execution reliability, semantic preservation, and static code metrics. Our evaluation focuses on translating C to Java, Python, and Rust, languages that follow distinct paradigms and represent alternatives to modernize C-based systems. We evaluate open-source LLMs using three prompting strategies to understand the impact on translation performance. Our findings highlight that while LLMs show promising results for simple code translation, their limitations regarding complex logic and distinct language paradigms require further analysis.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/marcovieira\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Marco Vieira\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/marcovieira/0656e0ba-1035-4355-9c1a-ab8a15b02b4b/micro-avatar?1783981324000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Marco Vieira<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of North Carolina at Charlotte</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/priyamashishshah\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Priyam Ashish Shah\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/priyamashishshah/305db563-fa61-4e72-bf29-12c01efeb6af/micro-avatar?1783971379000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Priyam Ashish <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>Shah<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of North Carolina at Charlotte</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/bhavainshah\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Bhavain Shah\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/bhavainshah/660b45d0-e2b3-40c7-8808-01aab0877ab1/micro-avatar?1783980390000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Bhavain Shah<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of North Carolina at Charlotte</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/rrezartakrasniqi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Rrezarta Krasniqi\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/rrezartakrasniqi/2360df7f-e1c5-42aa-b472-f31651ddaa20/micro-avatar?1783976599000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Rrezarta Krasniqi<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of North Carolina at Charlotte</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers/89/Polyglot-An-Extensible-Framework-to-Benchmark-Code-Translation-with-LLMs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-50b5f005-1185-4325-aac6-594189807b2b').modal